mapping "d3503.1" source="d3503" target="SNOMED_CT:288633005" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source d3503 SNOMED CT 288633005 = ICF d3503 Conversation with one person: the 4-level child of
        d350 for starting/sustaining/ending a dialogue with a single interlocutor. Target =, active RF2
        production (sv), SNOMED CT's direct observable for the conversation axis and the d350 parent.
        SNOMED CT's conversation children are about conversation stages
        (initiate/maintain/terminate/join/take turns) and contexts (different people/places/occasions),
        NOT about the number of interlocutors; no SNOMED CT concept distinguishes one-vs-many
        conversational partners. Ability to make conversation subsumes the conversation axis but the
        source's single-interlocutor specificity is outside any SNOMED CT child. Broader (low):
        conversation subsumes the conversation axis but the source's one-person-modality specificity is
        outside any SNOMED CT concept (deep climb, no narrower target); consistent with the
        leaf-under-broad-parent precedent (d3351/d3352 at). mapping_type=broader.
        """
}
mapping "d3504.1" source="d3504" target="SNOMED_CT:288694001" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source d3504 SNOMED CT 288694001 = ICF d3504 Conversation with many people: the 4-level child of
        d350 for carrying on a conversation with multiple interlocutors (a group). Target =, active RF2
        production, SNOMED CT's direct observable for the multi-interlocutor communication axis and a child
        of 288633005. Both denote the conversation-with-varied/multiple-people axis; SNOMED CT frames the
        ability to communicate across different people, ICF the activity of conversing with several.
        exact_match (high rather than): direct verified SNOMED CT observable match on the
        multi-interlocutor axis, but SNOMED CT's is marginally broader than ICF's (communication vs
        conversation; different-people vs many-at-once) — a small well-understood breadth mismatch on
        the same axis, per the d4301 one-level-breadth precedent. mapping_type=exact_match.
        """
}
